  - glue-qt 0.4.2 attaches a tool menu only to `DropdownTool` buttons and drops plain `Tool.menu_actions`, so the plan uses `SimpleToolMenu`. A non-checkable subtool deactivates the active mouse mode, so each subtool restores it.
- **Command line, autolink and Pixel caveats.**
  - `glue --startup` loads every window of every file (9 windows, 4.14 GB for 4000255147) and cannot stack scans, so WP9 documents the browser as the route for large or multi-scan observations.
  - With #2595 (M1), `add_datasets` may open the AutoLinkPreview modal during startup. Test for this, and add the links inside the action if needed.
  - A Pixel press forces Replace mode and writes into the edit subset, so a selected ROI subset is overwritten by the point.
  - Ctrl+K clears the point only when the layer tree has focus.
  - MDI subwindows do not reflow on resize, and tiling after maximise on a real macOS display is unverified.
