#### Notes and limits

- Each feature PR documents only its own capability. For example, WP4's quicklook PR adds the quicklook section, and WP1 PRs update the quoted labels and units. WP9 owns the cross-cutting guides, the corrections, the tutorial and the acceptance script. No doc claims that planned sessions, quicklook or science features already ship.
- Docs PRs go from a feature branch off `main`, and only when the user asks. Never stage the plan or `IRIS_PLAN_PROTOTYPES/` in them.
- The real-data checks (the acceptance script, the mask counts and the manual walk-throughs) need `~/DATA/IRIS` and cannot run in CI; CI covers the irispy 0.9.0 fixtures. Every run uses a micromamba env, an isolated HOME and the QSettings isolation.
- M0 event finding starts from the raster map. Stock SJI Pixel subsets give no raster spectrum on released core, even with `link_hpc`, so SJI clicks arrive in M1 through `wp1-m1-sji-to-raster`. #2595's native path would use frame-0 geometry, which is off by 78 SJI px across 4000255147.
- The frame-stepping crash (followup-2-1, followup-3-1) and the slider latency make the acceptance flow unusable until the WP10 M0 items land. The playback speed-up from repeated Forward presses is not discoverable, which is why WP9 documents it.
- `Time (Utc)` comes from glue core title-casing gWCS world axis names (`glue/core/coordinate_helpers.py:188-189`). No solar rename can restore "UTC"; only an optional upstream core change (WP0) can. User docs quote the displayed label only.
